date: 2026-10-03
timezone: America/Los_Angeles
release: forced second-Saturday release (started 2026-09-20; age 13)

This lifecycle marker records scheduled completion, not AAA acceptance.

Release gates: full Jest 27/27 suites and 483/483 tests pass. The exact-code
Chromium smoke passes at 320x568, 390x844, 844x390, 768x1024, 1440x900 and
3840x2160, including native touch, keyboard, pause/retry and mocked leaderboard
flow. No browser errors, external requests, failed local art or horizontal
overflow. Lead inspected all six Quench captures and opening-room phone,
landscape and desktop captures (4K downsampled). No glaring release blocker
was found. Evidence: node_modules/.cache/prism-warden/oct03-release-six/.

Final carried critic verdicts:
- Independent visual critic: scoped first-room SUN SEAL cue and 320/390 Quench
  framing PASS; overall AAA FAIL / OURS LOSES versus Nintendo's Link's Awakening.
  Scene hierarchy, environmental storytelling and 844x390 controls remain below
  the reference. This was a non-blind comparison, not a quality acceptance.
- Gameplay critic: AAA FAIL for encounter depth and scene hierarchy. The fresh
  Quench touch route reached Glass Edge, shut the valve and exited without a
  shot cut or Mirror return; that intended teaching cadence can be bypassed.
- Audio/VFX, human enjoyment, physical-device touch and performance: unaccepted.
- Independent AAA shipping judge: not run; this is a forced release.

Scope: five connected regions, 25 challenges, ten optional consequences, four
behavioral equipment choices, saved progress, restoration branches and a
three-phase Keeper rescue/evacuation finale are implemented. State-informed
native touch reached the full ending and optional discoveries, but this is
reachability evidence, not unaided human play or fun acceptance.

Carried debt: stronger screen-led learning and combat depth; Quench shot-cut and
return-shot bypass; distinct equipment decision value; scene hierarchy and
environmental storytelling; landscape control crowding and large-display UI
scale; independent audio/VFX listening and physical-device performance; human
novice play and enjoyment. No live leaderboard submission was performed in
verification. Do not reinterpret test or fixture results as AAA approval.
